{
  "$comment": "WAKE-UPS (lib/sessions/bus.ts watchSessions, trpc sessions.consume, lib/agents/triggers.ts, lib/agents/assistant-chat.ts memberChatsChanged). A session wakes ONLY on pending input: a person's message, another session's message or bus line (bus.json), an answered card, a trigger firing. Its device delivers pending input and CONSUMES it (`device.consume`); the watchdog nudges the host again while input stays pending (watchdog.json). WATCH (`send.watch`, `sessions_send {wakeOn}`): the watcher adds LIVE sessions of its team its account may see (shared, or its own user's), never itself; unknown, ended, foreign or private-to-another ids drop silently; idempotent. SCHEDULES fire into the agent OWNER's conversation with it as a user-authored, pending `trigger_fired` card (triggerId set, eventId null). The host scheduler decides which minutes are due (cron + tz, a first-seen trigger armed not fired, the window capped at rules.trigger.catchUpHours) and sends `trigger.schedule {due}`; the hub then: (1) skips the tick when it already fired once (`firedAt`) and nothing moved since the latest firing (no session in the agent's trees, i.e. the threads it started plus its conversations' children, has lastActivityAt after it; an agent with no tree always counts as moved; an Assistant counts every session of its member in the team except its own conversation root); (2) folds every due schedule into ONE card body (one copy.schedule line each, `caught up` when fired more than caughtUpAfterMinutes after the due minute); (3) NEVER STACKS: an unread tick card takes the new text in place (edit, no nudge); a read one no person message came after is edited and re-armed (pending again, nudged); otherwise a new card (nudged); (4) records `firedAt` per due trigger. EVENTS (`trigger.event`, an `events` row landing): every enabled event trigger on that name in the team fires a user-authored pending `trigger_fired` card (triggerId, eventId = the envelope id, name) into its owner's conversation, agents by id, never the agent whose own tree emitted it; each firing nudges.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "watch: live, same team, visible sessions only; never itself; idempotent",
      "given": {
        "sessions": [
          {
            "id": "w1",
            "userId": "u1"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1"
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "status": "ended",
            "endedAt": 0
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "teamId": "t2"
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "shared": false,
            "userId": "u2"
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "shared": false,
            "userId": "u1"
          }
        ]
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "event": {
            "kind": "send.watch",
            "at": 60000,
            "data": {
              "watcherId": "w1",
              "ids": [
                "s1",
                "s2",
                "s3",
                "s4",
                "s5",
                "w1",
                "nope"
              ]
            }
          },
          "effects": [],
          "result": {
            "sessionId": "w1"
          }
        },
        {
          "event": {
            "kind": "send.watch",
            "at": 120000,
            "data": {
              "watcherId": "w1",
              "ids": [
                "s1"
              ]
            }
          },
          "effects": [],
          "result": {
            "sessionId": "w1"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "sessions": {
          "w1": {
            "wakeOn": [
              "s1",
              "s5"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a pending message is the wake-up; the device consumes what it delivered",
      "given": {
        "sessions": [
          {
